ghost-role-information-citadel-service-name = Citadel Service
ghost-role-information-citadel-service-description = A Citadel service worker assigned to routine duties aboard the facility.
ghost-role-information-citadel-service-rules =
    You are a [color=#ff3db1][bold]Citadel resident[/bold][/color]. You are a service resident of the Citadel of the Khs'i-Ra Empire, sent 200 years ago to confirm Imperial control over this sector.
    However, having arrived in the sector recently, you noticed that the fleet that escorted you is missing, and the [color=#ff3db1]Governor[/color], ruler of the Citadel, has not yet arrived.
    After living in the sector for some time, you learned the new [color=#04bf5e]Andromeda Standard[/color] language and have a basic understanding of life in the sector.
    You are [color=red]forbidden[/color] to damage or destroy the [color=#ff3db1]Citadel[/color]. You are encouraged to keep the Citadel clean and orderly. Sector population may freely visit the Citadel if they do not harm it.
    You are [color=red]forbidden[/color] to loot the Citadel's inner vault. You must protect the vault from all outsiders, including Asakim. Only the [color=#ff3db1]Governor[/color] may lift this restriction.
    You are [color=red]not obligated[/color] to follow orders from the Eighth Expeditionary Fleet if they endanger the vault or its contents.
    Otherwise, you are free to do as you wish, including traveling across the sector, if you are confident the vault is protected.
    You [color=red]DO NOT REMEMBER[/color] your previous life or anything you learned as a ghost.